<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Dedicated small/status-bar icon for Axie GO's notifications.

  The status-bar "small icon" is NOT allowed to be the app's regular
  launcher icon — Android requires (and silently enforces) that it be a
  simple, flat, single-color stencil: opaque where the glyph is, fully
  transparent everywhere else. It then renders that shape as a plain white
  silhouette (tinted per-theme), throwing the source colors away entirely.

  Both notification services were passing @mipmap/ic_launcher — the full,
  multi-layer, full-color ADAPTIVE icon — as the small icon. Android can't
  turn that into a silhouette, so instead of erroring it falls back to its
  own generic placeholder glyph, tinted with the default notification
  color. That's the "wrong logo" — it was never actually rendering any of
  Axie GO's own artwork, adaptive-icon fix or not. The branded, full-color
  icon still shows correctly wherever the LARGE icon is used (see
  IconUtil.largeIcon), which is what the expanded notification shows.

  Shape here is a simple location pin, on-theme for a GPS walk/run tracker
  (echoes the pin already in the in-app logo) and simple enough to read
  clearly at 24dp.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
